//? Title: EfficientDet learned BiFPN fusion and shared separable heads
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Verify fast-normalized fusion and its gradients, odd-grid bidirectional pyramids and full D0 graph counts, then visibly fit every parameter of the compact source EfficientDet with paired BN-state checkpoints and actual digit scenes.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/efficientdet.cpp`.

> The method

EfficientDet combines feature-only EfficientNet, repeated weighted bidirectional feature pyramids and shared separable classification/regression towers. Learned fusion-edge scalars enter tensor optimization alongside convolution and normalization parameters.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/efficientdet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/efficientdet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/efficientdet_concept.tikz > build/efficientdet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/efficientdet_concept.svg build/efficientdet_concept.dvi > build/efficientdet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
