> Conclusion

The selected epoch21 has validation AP50 .037840. Test AP50 is .004607, AP75 is zero and AP50:95 is .000526, with800 detections. This bounded schedule generalizes poorly; the report retains the dense false positives and makes no architecture ranking from this tiny split.

Independent fusion derivatives and full D0 graph validation precede a bounded compact fit. Actual restored held-out boxes and measured AP document the instructional schedule; no pretrained detector or paper benchmark result is implied.

> References

- [Tan, Pang and Le (2020), EfficientDet: Scalable and Efficient Object Detection](https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.09070).
- [Authors’ EfficientDet implementation](https://github.com/google/automl/tree/master/efficientdet).
- [Lin et al. (2017), Focal Loss for Dense Object Detection](https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.02002).
